{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn `origin/main` at `c019920390926d543a0813d4c0c8721543d98776`, the `review_interrupts_signal_unavailable` alarm description in `infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf` says “1-datapoint latch,” but the resource is configured as a 2-of-4 evaluation window. The heredoc is an executable Terraform value, so correcting it is outside comment-only remediation.\n\n## Approach\nMake the alarm description state the configured evaluation rule and add a focused assertion that description and resource settings cannot drift.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The alarm description accurately states the configured 2-of-4 window.\n- [x] A focused test fails if the prose and `datapoints_to_alarm`/`evaluation_periods` diverge.\n- [x] Terraform format/validate, focused monitoring tests, lint, and typecheck pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788756422937577001,"uuid":"a5441303-fba0-4949-a75b-a48dfc265a66"}